		},
		"negotiation": "a first row (arm negotiation) records whether the origin saw Available-Dictionary and served dcz; the windows run only when it did",
		"files": "a real pair of JavaScript aggregates from one Drupal site, a dictionary and the aggregate served on a later page of the same visit; the page fetches the target and reads its bytes without running it",
		"why not a stylesheet": "no stylesheet pair of the sizing corpus had a dictionary that beat plain brotli by a margin the encode could show; the churned JavaScript aggregates did",
		"cache": "every load asks for a new query string, which the dictionary match ignores, so no load is a cache hit"
	},
